# shellcheck shell=bash
# Invocation behind output/evaluation/determinism/cpu_8978759/, the CPU arm
# of the determinism check (hpc/submit_determinism_cpu.sh).
#
# Job 8978759 (determinism_cpu, account <project-b>), 2026-10-04, 04:51:19
# to 06:08:35 BST by sacct, ran with these values from the ARC clone
# ~/paper_speech_transcription_audit_w2b at f2578b8, with no modified
# tracked file by its environment record. It ran on htc-c074, an AMD EPYC
# 9634 84-Core Processor (cpu.txt), in float32 with 16 threads and no GPU,
# and wrote into repro/cpu_arm/determinism_cpu/ under
# $DATA/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/. Its log is
# logs/determinism_cpu_8978759.out in that clone. A repeat and a second
# seed agreed with its first decode on 200 of 200 utterances. Its
# summaries, cpu.txt and WER report are committed in
# output/evaluation/determinism/cpu_8978759/, and
# determinism_cross_accelerator.json compares its hypotheses, which stay in
# that ARC directory, with the GPU runs under the label cpu.
#
# The values are those of the GPU runs in determinism.env (jobs 8554985 and
# 8781724): suite ami, the first 200 test utterances, seeds 0 and 1, and two
# decodes of seed 0, so the arm's seed0_run1.csv covers the same 200
# utterances, under the same seed, as job 8781724's (NVIDIA L40S). The
# script decodes seed 1 once, where those jobs also decoded it a second
# time. What changes against the GPU runs is the hardware, a processor in
# place of a GPU with no CUDA beneath it, and the precision, float32 in
# place of the checkpoint's float16 (transcription.py also decodes in
# float32 on a machine without CUDA). The arm ran later code than they
# did, but its decode path differs from theirs only in the steps
# determinism_cross_accelerator_runs.json lists for 6f9bf56 and in the
# --device and --dtype options it passes.
#
# Reproduce (from the repository root on ARC):
#   ( set -a; . hpc/runs/determinism_cpu.env || exit 1; set +a
#     sbatch --account='<your-project>' hpc/submit_determinism_cpu.sh )
#
# The job writes into $REPORT_DIR/determinism_cpu/, away from every GPU
# run's files. Job 8978759 wrote into the directory this record named
# before it ran, given below as the original. REPORT_DIR now sends a
# reproduction to repro/determinism_cpu/, so it cannot overwrite the ARC
# copy of that run, which submit_determinism_cpu.sh would also refuse to
# do (exit 3, before any decode) unless OVERWRITE=1.
# original: REPORT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/repro/cpu_arm"
DET_SUITE=ami
DET_LIMIT=200
DET_SEEDS="0 1"
DET_REPEATS=2
DET_DTYPE=float32
REPORT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/repro/determinism_cpu"
